          "question": "Provide a complete, self-contained proof of the Heine-Cantor Theorem using the Bolzano-Weierstrass theorem for sequences:\nIf $f: K \\to \\mathbb{R}$ is continuous on a compact set $K \\subset \\mathbb{R}$, then $f$ is uniformly continuous on $K$.",
          "statement": "Provide a complete, self-contained proof of the Heine-Cantor Theorem using the Bolzano-Weierstrass theorem for sequences:\nIf $f: K \\to \\mathbb{R}$ is continuous on a compact set $K \\subset \\mathbb{R}$, then $f$ is uniformly continuous on $K$.",
